+## What I learned that the next session needs
+- **Ollama memory:** the box had ~5.7 GiB free; Ollama's default 128k-context estimate demands 11-16 GiB
+  → HTTP 500. Fix = `options.num_ctx=2048` + `llama3.2:3b`. With that it enriches fine (~2-5s/resume warm).
+  8B won't fit until more RAM is free. Graceful degrade (→deterministic, needs_review) works when it can't load.
+- **liteparse:** Python pkg v2.0.0, `LiteParse(quiet=True, ocr_enabled=False).parse(path).text`. OCR disabled
+  on purpose (no Tesseract installed → only stderr noise). PDF=liteparse, DOCX=mammoth, old `.doc`=needs
+  LibreOffice (2 files degrade to filename-only).
+- **Paste messiness:** SEC pastes are clean result lists; the GSA paste includes the left filter sidebar
+  ("Boolean search", clearance-filter labels) and multi-page headers → scrubbed by `_is_junk_paste` in run.py.
+- **Current-vs-prior employer:** `canonical_company` scans whole resume text, so a *prior* Booz stint can set
+  `company`. Acceptable (matcher also reads `prior_companies`); `company` shows canonical-only (raw → source_metadata).
+- **Matcher gate (the key tuning decision):** a contact matches a program only with a BD reason —
+  employer ∈ {prime, competitor subs}, OR PoP-city + title both hit, OR `program_hint`. This keeps the ~290
+  bulk paste results tight, but it parks skill-relevant **resumes** (AFRL/ISR/GEOINT people not at a competitor
+  and not in a PoP metro) in the *unmatched* bucket. They ARE listed in `HUMINT_SUMMARY.md` with full context.
+
+## Open follow-up decisions for the user (NOT done — need a call)
+1. **Resume matcher gate:** loosen for the resume lane so strong title/skills + clearance can qualify a
+   curated resume even without employer/PoP? (Trade-off: surfaces ISR/AFRL resume leads onto sheets vs.
+   risks cyber-people matching every cyber program.) Could be lane-aware + a "skills-match" signal.
+2. **Per-resume program intent:** resumes have no `program_hint`. If the user tagged each downloaded resume
+   with the program they pulled it for, matching gets much sharper. Add a `program_hint` column to the
+   resume entries in `intake_allowlist.json`.
+3. **Graph sync (spec Phase 6, deferred):** upsert Contacts/edges into a LOCAL graph (Neo4j :7687 / local AGE,
+   NEVER pg-pts). Not built yet.
+4. **Bullhorn load:** `bullhorn_candidate_id` is null; downstream `pts-bullhorn-loader` can ingest the
+   canonical JSON when desired.
+
+## How to run
+```
+python3 -m clearancejobs_pipeline.run                 # deterministic, fast
+python3 -m clearancejobs_pipeline.run --ollama        # + local llama3.2:3b enrichment
+python3 -m clearancejobs_pipeline.run --skip-intake   # reuse already-copied intake/
+python3 -m clearancejobs_pipeline.run --config <_contract_config.json> --out <dir>   # different prime
+python3 -m pytest clearancejobs_pipeline/tests/ -q    # 71 tests
+```
+Add a person: add a named entry to `clearancejobs_pipeline/intake_allowlist.json` (NEVER glob Downloads).
